  "body": "MAINLINE-043 supplement folds both MAINLINE-041 frequency-5 closure witnesses alongside frozen 022d. QUESTIONABLE / PROJECTION; actual member/frame/lifetime probabilities remain null.\n\nEach f5 point has 750 members and 1500 end interfaces. Actual lengths and correlated force/moment arrays reproduce target peak compression 1.164235/1.145748 GPa at q=1.143285/1.083205. Positive longitudinal tension remains zero in these ideal fields, without resolving local multiaxial stress.\n\nFor hypothetical compression m=10 and common whole-member scale 3.9 GPa, summed per-member peak envelopes give own-screen frame Pf 0.00252417/0.00214283. Required common scales for frame Pf 1e-3/1e-6 are 4.27868/8.53751 GPa (5%) and 4.20909/8.39866 GPa (019). A 1 cm3 calibration instead gives Pf 0.991133/0.979046. No catalogue-to-full-member qualification is implied.\n\nAt common 022d q=1.258252, peaks rise to 1.285383/1.337950 GPa and whole-member-hypothesis Pf to 0.00672419/0.00992957; these loads exceed the new source screens. Total volume changes little despite smaller members; surface area increases 18.44%/17.04%. Strength/scatter, tensile-size and proof comparisons are filed.\n\n041's local-wall sensitivity remains 1.033223/0.978132; its sub-unity 019 result is not hidden by fracture projections. Material, joint, instability and lifetime NFIs remain unclosed.\n\nTwenty-six input pins, 843 scientific checks and 77 packaging checks pass. One admitted job released. All 96 original 043 artifacts remain unchanged. Fold complete; no successor named; SLEEPING.",
